llab><year>2008</year><comment>Health impact evaluation of Ethiopia's national response to HIV/AIDS, tuberculosis and malaria. 2007. Addis Ababa (Ethiopia): Ethiopian Health and Nutrition Research Institute</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000056-Ethiopian9"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>Ethiopian Ministry of Health</collab><year>2008</year><comment>Health and health related indicators 2006/2007. Addis Ababa (Ethiopia): Ministry of Health</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000056-United1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>United Nations Children's Fund</collab><year>2008</year><article-title>Ethiopia statistics: Basic indicators.</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.unicef.org/infobycountry/ethiopia_statistics.html">http://www.unicef.org/infobycountry/ethiopia_statistics.html</ext-link>. Accessed 10 February 2009</comment></citation></ref></ref-list><glossary><title>Abbreviations</title><def-list><def-item><term>ART</term><def><p>antiretroviral treatment</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>HRH</term><def><p>human resources for health</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>NGO</term><def><p>nongovernmental organization</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>PEPFAR</term><def><p>President's Emergency Plan for AIDS Relief</p></def></def-item></def-list></glossary><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p>The authors received no funding for this work.</p></fn><fn fn-type="other"><p><bold>Provenance:</bold> Not commissioned; externally peer reviewed</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>